
# Speaker Guide: Product Deep Dive

## Session overview

This session explores how GitHub is evolving to support an agent-native software development lifecycle, where humans and AI agents collaborate to plan, build, verify, and deliver software.

The session covers GitHub's investment in platform scalability, connected Copilot experiences, agent orchestration, enterprise governance, AI-powered security, and measuring the outcomes of agent-driven development.

**Core message:** As agents take on more development work, GitHub is evolving every layer of the platform to support them. The goal isn't simply to generate more code or consume more tokens, but to help developers complete valuable work faster, securely, and at scale.

### Before you present

- Review the presentation deck and embedded speaker notes.
- Familiarise yourself with GitHub's engineering investments, Copilot runtime, Memory, Dreaming, Fusion, Cloud Sandboxes, and enterprise governance capabilities.
- Review the product announcements and confirm the availability of features marked GA or preview.
